{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '260,520p' docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-vm.md\"","aggregated_output":"### B4: effects, streams, and continuations\n\n    New: test/yin/vm/debruijn_vm_effects_test.cljc\n    Existing edits: none unless an already published data-only helper is\n    factored without semantic change\n\nAdd stream operations, primitives, FFI, gensym, macro-expanded forms,\n`current-continuation`, park, and resume.  Completion requires parity for\nobservable outcomes and store transitions.  Cross-engine continuation\ntransport remains deferred until UCF is implemented.\n\n### B5: differential integration and persistence adapter\n\n    New: test/yin/vm/debruijn_vm_parity_test.cljc\n    Existing edits: none\n\nRun every existing semantic, engine, parity, linearize, and VM fixture through\nboth executable paths.  Add a narrow adapter from a projected fingerprint to\nthe code-image cache only if the owner approves persistence.  Completion\nrequires JVM, Node/CLJS, and ClojureDart parity, kondo clean, cljstyle clean,\nand proof that named storage and named consumers are unchanged.\n\n### B6: optional transport integration\n\n    New files only, after an owner decision\n    Existing edits: none by default\n\nIntegrate with DaoJing or UCF only after their respective contracts are\napproved.  This phase is not required to ship the local de Bruijn VM.\n\n## 7. Test matrix and non-goals\n\nThe acceptance matrix includes:\n\n    Area                  Required rows\n    --------------------  -----------------------------------------------\n    Projection input      every node tag, literals, vectors/lists, refs\n    Scope                 shadowing, deep frames, duplicate params, bad pair\n    Calls                 zero/one/many params, nil fill, extras dropped\n    Control               if, labels, evaluation order, tail calls\n    Streams               make, put, cursor, next, close, blocked, gaps\n    VM effects            store, gensym, primitives, registry, FFI\n    Continuations         current, park, resume, local continuation parity\n    Macros                expanded macro forms and unexpanded diagnostics\n    DAG                   shared node in equal and different contexts\n    Identity              alpha-equivalent same fingerprint, free rename diff\n    Integrity             deterministic image bytes on JVM, Node, and Dart\n    Differential          all existing semantic/parity fixtures on both VMs\n    Safety                malformed records and invalid scope are diagnostics\n\nFor each differential row compare result, error classification, effects,\nstream outcomes, store, and terminal/blocked status.  Do not compare source\nids, instruction locations, closure allocation identity, or debug text.\n\nThe project does not include equality saturation or an optimiser, a new JIT\nbeyond the allowances in `yin.vm.jit.md`, global distribution, dependency\nresolution by hash, or any change to the projection or its fingerprint.\n\n## 8. Risks and owner decisions\n\nThe main risk is an accidental claim that a hash-consed record is a reusable\ncode block.  B2 therefore duplicates occurrences until a lexical calling\nconvention is specified.  Other risks are malformed scope pairs, loss of\nnamed source diagnostics, differences in host numeric or FFI values, and the\nfact that UCF is not yet an implemented transport contract.\n\nThe following are owner decisions, not silent architectural choices:\n\n- approve the `:yin.debruijn.code/*` namespace and descriptor;\n- approve occurrence duplication as the first lowering strategy;\n- decide whether code images are persisted in a new DaoJing envelope or kept\n  as a cache artifact;\n- decide whether and when UCF must support cross-host continuation transport;\n- decide whether the optional node-hash debug field is exposed to users;\n- confirm the exact structural tail propagation for every stream application;\n- decide whether the sibling VM implements existing VM protocols immediately;\n- decide whether a source-to-projected lineage index is ever persisted.\n\nRouting recommendation: implement B0 through B5 on the refreshed Claude pool,\nreview each phase with a different model family, and reserve GPT for\narchitectural sign-off.  Do not route review to Gemini or agy while their\ncapacity is constrained.\n\n## 9. What this design must not change\n\nThe AST schema, AST walker, named emitter, named linearizer, semantic VM,\nexisting `:yin.code/*` dimension, `dao.stream` protocols, lease layer, waitset,\nnamed storage, projection algorithm, and fingerprint remain unchanged.  The\nnew VM is an additional interpreter and code dimension.  Any future change to\none of those authorities requires its own design and review.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
